  "depends_on": ["O2", "O4", "S1"],
  "factor_sequence": ["O2", "S1", "O4"],
  "proposed_b": [
    {
      "statement": "The boundary ∂G of the hyperbolic tiling {p,q} in S1 is a finite graph with a well-defined total boundary area A_∂, measured in units of l_P^2, and the Hilbert space ℋ_∂G satisfies O2: dim(ℋ_∂G) ~ exp(A_∂/(4 l_P^2)).",
      "motivation": "This closes the gap δ by explicitly extending the area-law dimension scaling (O2) to the boundary system itself, using the geometric structure from S1. It makes H0 directly provable.",
      "depends_on": ["O2", "S1"],
      "factor_sequence": ["S1", "O2"]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The holographic isometry Φ in O4, when realized as the perfect tensor network from S1, is a bijection between ℋ_bulk and ℋ_∂G (i.e., an isomorphism), not just an isometry.",
      "motivation": "If Φ is an isomorphism, then dim(ℋ_bulk) = dim(ℋ_∂G). Combining with O2 applied to the bulk (as a region with boundary area equal to the total boundary area of the tiling, per S1) would directly yield H0. This strengthens O4 within the S1 model.",
      "depends_on": ["O4", "S1"],
      "factor_sequence": ["S1", "O4"]
    },
