    "motivation": "This directly bridges O2 (which gives bulk dimension scaling with area) and S1's geometric structure. If proven, then combined with O4 (isometry), we get dim(ℋ_∂G) ≥ exp(total_boundary_area/(4 l_P^2)), which is half of H0. The other direction (upper bound) would require additional constraints.",
